# GitHub Pages File Structure Rules

## CRITICAL: HTML File Placement for GitHub Pages

When creating or modifying HTML files for this repository's GitHub Pages:

  ### ✅ REQUIRED STRUCTURE
ALL HTML files MUST follow this exact structure:
```
/docs/[project-name]/index.html
  ```

  ### 📋 RULES
  1. Create a folder directly under `/docs/` with your project name
2. Inside that folder, create `index.html` as the main file
3. URL will be: `https://diceman-hub.github.io/ino-moneycoach/[project-name]/`

### ❌ NEVER DO THIS
  - `/docs/project-name.html` ← Wrong! This creates URLs with .html extension
- `/docs/folder/subfolder/project/index.html` ← Wrong! Too many levels
- `/docs/project-name/main.html` ← Wrong! Must be named index.html

  ### ✅ CORRECT EXAMPLES
  - `/docs/sfc-dashboard/index.html` → URL: `/sfc-dashboard/`
  - `/docs/credit-card/index.html` → URL: `/credit-card/`
  - `/docs/budget-tracker/index.html` → URL: `/budget-tracker/`

  ### 📝 IMPORTANT NOTES
  - Always use lowercase, hyphenated folder names
- Each project gets its own folder
- The file inside MUST be named `index.html`
  - This structure ensures clean URLs without .html extensions
- See /docs/README.md for detailed guidelines

## Git push

When running `git push` (to any remote, e.g. ino-moneycoach or origin), **always** use `required_permissions: ["all"]`. Otherwise the process cannot access the credential helper / Keychain and push will fail with "could not read Username" or "Device not configured". Do not use only `network` + `git_write`.
